      "content": "i see. so when historians look at the different narratives, do they treat them both as equally valid historical perspectives, or is one side's argument usually seen as more factually grounded or backed by more international legitimacy? like, is there a difference in how the \"right to the land\" is viewed from an academic standpoint?",
