      "content": "Academically, most historians treat both narratives as valid *perspectives* stemming from deeply held national experiences rather than declaring one version of history unilaterally \"correct.\" While international bodies and treaties have supported certain outcomes (like UN resolutions), historians analyze the underlying legal, demographic, and geopolitical factors supporting both claims. The academic approach focuses on analyzing *how* each side constructs its claim, rather than adjudicating its ultimate truth.",
